# Admin settings — selectable option cards

When building **selectable option grids** in admin or settings (themes, voices, chrome looks, free-session looks, avatars, layouts, etc.), use the **AI Voice picker** pattern — not border-only selection.

## Reference

- Component: `app/components/admin/AdminVoicePicker.tsx`
- CSS: `.admin-voice-card` / `.admin-voice-check` / `.admin-voice-check.is-on` in `app/globals.css`
- Also applied on: `GuidedChatChromePicker`, `FreeSessionChromePicker` (reuse `.admin-voice-check`)

## Required pattern

1. **Radiogroup** — wrap the grid in `role="radiogroup"` with an `aria-label`.
2. **Per option** — each card is selectable via `role="radio"` + `aria-checked` (button or select control).
3. **Radio indicator** — circular control **top-right** of the card:
   - Unselected: empty circle (`.admin-voice-check`)
   - Selected: filled sage with mint inset (`.admin-voice-check.is-on`)
4. **Selected card chrome** — light mint background + sage border (same as `.admin-voice-card.is-selected`), not border-only and not a checkbox.
5. Prefer **reusing** `.admin-voice-check` / `.is-on` / selected card styles over inventing a new indicator.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — AI Voice style
<article className={`…-card${selected ? " is-selected" : ""}`}>
  <button type="button" role="radio" aria-checked={selected} …>
    <span className={`admin-voice-check${selected ? " is-on" : ""}`} aria-hidden />
    …
  </button>
</article>

// ❌ BAD — border/ring only, no radio
<button className={selected ? "is-selected" : ""} aria-pressed={selected} />
```

## Do not

- Use checkboxes for single-select option grids
- Rely on border/shadow alone to show the active choice
- Invent a third selection language for the same admin surface
